  "verbalization": "Agallochin F is implicated in the regulation of SNB-78 through a multi-step mechanism involving protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. This pathway is supported by multiple evidence chains, each linking Agallochin F to a compound that targets SNB-78. The first evidence chain connects Agallochin F directly to Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is then targeted by Ginsenoside R10, and finally by the compound [(3S,10S,13R,17R)-17-(5-ethyl-6-methylhept-6-en-2-yl)-4,10,13,14-tetramethyl-1,2,3,4,5,6,9,11,12,15,16,17-dodecahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-yl] acetate, which also targets SNB-78. The second evidence chain provides a more detailed molecular profile of the compound, reinforcing the pathway's validity. The third evidence chain links Agallochin F to Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is also targeted by 6-C-Methylquercetin 3-methyl ether, further supporting the role of this enzyme in SNB-78 regulation. The integrated evidence suggests that Agallochin F modulates SNB-78 through the inhibition of protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, potentially by interfering with signaling pathways that regulate cell proliferation or survival. The consistent presence of multiple targets and their shared involvement in SNB-78 regulation strengthens the mechanistic link, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
